    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d741">

                <pb facs="0833" n="748" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg748"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860c.4016/49: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Poland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d741-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1919-05-17T16:23:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1919-05-04T00:00:00+03:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 17,
                            1919, 4.23 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Department’s 1797 [<hi rendition="#italic">1727</hi>] April 25, 2 p.m.,
                    received May 3, both reports referred to in Department’s telegram inaccurate.
                    Committee composed of both Poles and Jews appointed by Polish Diet has <pb
                        facs="0834" n="749" xml:id="pg749"/> just returned from making investigation
                    on the ground. Some 400 pages of testimony taken and now being digested. I am
                    promised full reply as soon as it is ready and shall report further.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
